nyx-gestures 2.1.0

Touchpad gestures for GNOME Wayland.

Recommended setup (one command): ./install.sh
  - daemon: libinput-gestures + nyx-keyd (libei key injection), 2 procs, ~32 MB.
    Performs every gesture action. Works on any GNOME/Wayland version and any
    touchpad, including X11.
  - suppressor: GNOME Shell extension (nyx-native-suppress@nyx.local). Disables
    ONLY GNOME's native swipe trackers so they cannot double-fire with the
    daemon. Handles no gestures, injects no keys, patches no system files.

The old extension-only handler in extension/ (get_gesture_motion_delta based,
GNOME 45+) is experimental reference material and is NOT installed by default.
--backend=ext is a deprecated alias that installs the recommended daemon+suppressor
combo with a warning.

Neither path patches a system binary. There are no apt hooks.

Gesture map (daemon)
  3F swipe left/right  tile window to left/right half (super+Left/Right)
  3F swipe up          app switcher (super+Tab)
  3F swipe down        keyboard resize (alt+F8; arrows + Esc)
  4F swipe left/right  switch workspace (super+alt+Right/Left)
  4F swipe up          fullscreen (alt+F9)
  4F swipe down        show desktop (alt+F12)
  3F pinch out/in      screenshot (file+clipboard) / close window
  4F pinch out/in      screenshot picker / show desktop

Requirements
  daemon   python3, python-evdev, python-libei (private venv). Root for /usr/local.
  suppressor  GNOME 45+. No root: extension installs per-user.
  both     a touchpad with at least 4 slots for 4-finger gestures.

Logging
  ~/.local/state/nyx-gestures/nyx.log (rotated 256 KiB). Level via:
    gsettings set org.gnome.shell.extensions.nyx-gestures level debug
  nyx-keyd logs to the user journal: journalctl --user -u nyx-keyd
  Self-heal: after 4 consecutive session failures the injector exits so
  systemd restarts it with a fresh libei/GDBus connection.

Diagnosis
  ./install.sh --doctor       read-only, safe on any machine
  ./lib/nyx-preflight.sh      platform capability report

Tests (working tree only, not shipped)
  node dev/decisiontest.js libinput-gestures.conf   28 checks, no GNOME needed
  ./testrig.sh                                      headless GNOME shell gates
    (includes SUPPRESS_ASSERT: re-enable regression, fixed in 2.1.0)
